From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ws2_32: Ask for a receive buffer of at least 1 MiB.

A game sets SO_RCVBUF to 32 KiB on its UDP socket and stops reading it
while it loads a map. The PS5's BSD network stack drops datagrams that
do not fit, counting each one's whole storage against the limit; Windows
and Linux leave more room. An Unreal Engine game joining a dedicated
server loses the replication data the server sends during the load, and
the server gives up on the connection: the join times out.

setsockopt( SO_RCVBUF ) now asks for at least 1 MiB, and sets the
requested size as before if the system refuses that.
---
 dlls/ws2_32/socket.c | 17 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ws2_32/socket.c b/dlls/ws2_32/socket.c
--- a/dlls/ws2_32/socket.c
+++ b/dlls/ws2_32/socket.c
@@ -3300,7 +3300,10 @@
     else
         return n;
 }
+
 
+/* The smallest receive buffer setsockopt( SO_RCVBUF ) asks for. */
+#define MIN_RCVBUF (1024 * 1024)
 
 static int server_setsockopt( SOCKET s, ULONG code, const char *optval, int optlen )
 {
@@ -3392,6 +3395,20 @@
 
         case SO_RCVBUF:
             if (optlen < 0) optlen = 4;
+            /* A BSD stack drops what does not fit the buffer, counting each datagram's whole storage against it,
+             * where Windows and Linux leave more room. A game that asks for a small buffer and then stops reading
+             * while it loads loses the server's data. Ask for at least MIN_RCVBUF; keep the game's size if the
+             * system refuses. */
+            if (optval && optlen >= sizeof(value))
+            {
+                memcpy( &value, optval, sizeof(value) );
+                if (value < MIN_RCVBUF)
+                {
+                    value = MIN_RCVBUF;
+                    if (!server_setsockopt( s, IOCTL_AFD_WINE_SET_SO_RCVBUF, (char *)&value, sizeof(value) ))
+                        return 0;
+                }
+            }
             return server_setsockopt( s, IOCTL_AFD_WINE_SET_SO_RCVBUF, optval, optlen );
 
         case SO_RCVTIMEO:
